WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.360
<b>Koone Girls' Academy</b>

00:04.730 --> 00:07.740
<b>Final Exam Scores</b>

00:04.730 --> 00:07.740
<b>Adashino Oto</b>

00:04.730 --> 00:07.740
<b>Ametsuchi Nodoka</b>

00:05.490 --> 00:08.120
Adashino-san got a perfect score again.

00:08.120 --> 00:09.960
She's a world away from us.

00:09.960 --> 00:13.620
Ametsuchi-san is amazing, too! 
Those two are always the top scorers.

00:13.940 --> 00:17.820
Her father is the head of 
Takamagahara Hospital, right?

00:17.820 --> 00:20.270
It sounds like excellence runs in the family.

00:24.380 --> 00:27.100
Exams are finally over!

00:27.100 --> 00:29.710
They were pretty tough this time.

00:29.710 --> 00:32.580
I'm just glad none of us need 
to take make-up exams.

00:32.580 --> 00:34.140
Y'know what?

00:34.850 --> 00:37.270
That study session was 
worth having after all!

00:37.690 --> 00:38.580
Yeah.

00:38.580 --> 00:42.270
And that's why we should celebrate 
making it through our tests!

00:42.270 --> 00:44.530
You have some good ideas from time to time.

00:44.530 --> 00:46.040
From time to Tama time.

00:46.040 --> 00:47.530
That was pretty bad.

00:47.530 --> 00:50.710
I'd like to hear Nodoka sing again. 
It's been too long.

00:50.710 --> 00:54.450
Occhan, I love you! Let's go do karaoke!

00:54.450 --> 00:55.430
Yeah.

00:55.430 --> 00:57.040
Let's go!

01:01.620 --> 01:06.420
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

01:01.620 --> 01:06.420
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:28.330 --> 02:33.260
<b>Dreams, Dance, and a Tsukumogami</b>

02:28.330 --> 02:33.260
<b>Dreams, Dance, and a Tsukumogami</b>

02:33.260 --> 02:38.510
<i>No matter where you are, 
I'm yelling my support for you</i>

02:38.830 --> 02:41.570
<i>Smile and catch your dream</i>

02:41.570 --> 02:44.830
<i>Grab it and go beyond it</i>

02:50.170 --> 02:52.870
<i>Like the sea at night,</i>

02:52.870 --> 02:55.280
<i>There's only the faintest of light</i>

02:55.280 --> 02:58.590
<i>But even if we can't see into the distance,</i>

03:01.040 --> 03:03.810
<i>We'll shut down the things we don't like,</i>

03:03.810 --> 03:06.290
<i>Trust in tomorrow,</i>

03:06.570 --> 03:10.700
<i>And upgrade toward our ideals</i>

03:07.000 --> 03:09.790
One snack basket, please.

03:11.550 --> 03:17.160
<i>Please don't lose sight 
of your prismatic dream</i>

03:17.160 --> 03:22.180
<i>Lock on to that rainbow-colored light</i>

03:22.640 --> 03:31.230
<i>When you're feeling weak, just think of me</i>

03:33.570 --> 03:38.820
<i>No matter where you are, 
I'm yelling my support for you</i>

03:39.190 --> 03:41.830
<i>I want to always be here for you</i>

03:41.830 --> 03:44.580
<i>Holding out my hand to you</i>

03:44.580 --> 03:49.830
<i>No matter where you are, 
I'm yelling my support for you</i>

03:46.380 --> 03:49.830
One more strawberry sundae, please.

03:49.830 --> 03:52.670
<i>Smile and catch your dream</i>

03:52.670 --> 03:55.950
<i>Grab it and go beyond it</i>

03:57.130 --> 03:59.110
Yay! That was amazing!

03:59.110 --> 04:01.900
Occhan, what did you think of my singing?

04:03.700 --> 04:04.430
Huh?

04:05.500 --> 04:07.940
You weren't listening!

04:08.790 --> 04:11.600
See you later! Bye-bye!

04:11.940 --> 04:14.140
See you tomorrow!

04:24.030 --> 04:25.330
<b>Takamagahara Hospital</b>

04:31.350 --> 04:33.030
Good day, Shirai-san.

04:33.030 --> 04:34.890
Oh, Nodoka-san!

04:34.890 --> 04:37.070
I'd like to see my dad if I can.

04:37.070 --> 04:39.190
Just a second.

04:39.500 --> 04:42.170
The chairman is in a meeting right now.

04:42.170 --> 04:45.970
Then could you give this to my dad, please?

04:45.970 --> 04:47.600
Your test scores?

04:47.600 --> 04:50.480
Of course. I'll make sure he gets them.

04:50.480 --> 04:51.710
If you would, please.

04:52.100 --> 04:55.340
And please don't look at them, Shirai-san.

04:55.800 --> 04:56.860
Understood.

05:07.390 --> 05:09.870
Welcome home, Nodoka-san.

05:09.870 --> 05:12.520
A good day to you, Kotaka-sensei.

05:13.700 --> 05:16.200
Let's get started as soon 
as you've changed clothes.

05:16.200 --> 05:18.380
Our time is limited, after all.

05:18.380 --> 05:19.600
Yes.

05:21.550 --> 05:25.060
This problem looks complex at first glance,

05:25.060 --> 05:27.950
but it simply requires a combination 
of the methods I taught you last time.

05:29.160 --> 05:32.140
Yes, that's it! Splendid!

05:32.700 --> 05:36.760
There aren't many middle schoolers who can 
solve problems from UTokyo's Science Dept. III.

05:39.990 --> 05:42.320
Well, let's stop here for today.

05:42.700 --> 05:44.310
You've worked hard.

05:44.640 --> 05:45.410
Okay.

05:45.720 --> 05:50.660
Everyone hopes that you will one day 
take over running Takamagahara Hospital.

05:50.660 --> 05:54.360
I'm certain you will be able 
to rise to those expectations.

05:57.100 --> 05:59.220
Let's do our best tomorrow, as well.

05:59.220 --> 06:01.300
Thank you very much.

06:06.550 --> 06:08.060
This is no fun!

06:08.400 --> 06:09.560
It's no fun!

06:09.560 --> 06:13.210
No fun! No fun! No fun!

06:20.570 --> 06:22.190
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

06:20.570 --> 06:22.190
<b>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hTo Students and Parents

Creating social media accounts or accounts
on video sites for the purpose of hosting
livestreams or uploading videos is prohibited.

Livestreams and/or videos can only be watched
with a parent or guardian's permission,
subject to a daily viewing limit at their discretion.</b>

06:34.480 --> 06:36.860
<i>Can you hear me, all you small fry?</i>

06:37.120 --> 06:41.590
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

06:37.230 --> 06:41.590
<i>This is the mermaid VTuber, Himeuo Yorumun!</i>

06:37.410 --> 06:41.590
<b>Himeuo Yorumun</b>

06:42.820 --> 06:44.840
Good evening, Yoru-chan!

06:45.190 --> 06:47.950
<i>How did you all spend your day?</i>

06:47.950 --> 06:52.230
<i>I was busy with work the whole time!</i>

06:52.230 --> 06:54.350
<i>I'm one exhausted lady.</i>

06:54.650 --> 06:58.870
<i>Huh? Whoever said, "For a lady, you're a 
little lacking up there," I'll send you flying!</i>

06:59.200 --> 07:02.380
<i>Oh, right! Remember the merch 
I released a while ago?</i>

07:02.380 --> 07:04.990
<i>It looks like it's started 
arriving at your homes!</i>

07:04.990 --> 07:06.490
Yeah! I bought some!

07:06.490 --> 07:11.430
<i>The truth is, I'd like to release 
a sexy boobs mouse pad,</i>

07:11.430 --> 07:14.470
<i>but for some reason, my manager 
keeps shooting down the idea.</i>

07:14.470 --> 07:17.000
<i>I guess that's fair. I </i>am<i> an idol and all.</i>

07:17.300 --> 07:21.500
<i>So for now, you'll have to be satisfied with 
acrylic keychains and body pillow covers.</i>

07:22.170 --> 07:26.010
<i>Hey! All of you who just said "flat as 
a cutting board"! I'm blocking you!</i>

07:27.260 --> 07:27.890
<b></b>Sorry

07:27.730 --> 07:29.810
<i>You're sending super chats to apologize?</i>

07:27.880 --> 07:28.510
<b></b>Sorry

07:27.890 --> 07:28.510
<b></b>My apologies.

07:28.510 --> 07:29.130
<b></b>Sorry

07:28.510 --> 07:29.130
<b></b>My apologies.

07:28.510 --> 07:29.140
<b></b>Soz

07:29.130 --> 07:29.760
<b></b>Soz

07:29.140 --> 07:29.760
<b></b>I'm sorry. I won't do it again. Please have mercy

07:29.760 --> 07:31.220
<b></b>I'm sorry. I won't do it again. Please have mercy

07:29.760 --> 07:31.220
<b></b>I'm sorry. I just got caught up in the flow

07:29.810 --> 07:33.340
<i>I was joking! Please don't take it seriously!</i>

07:31.220 --> 07:32.260
<b></b>I'm sorry. I just got caught up in the flow

07:32.260 --> 07:34.390
<b></b>I'm sorry. I just got caught up in the flow

07:33.340 --> 07:35.550
<i>Everyone, treat your money 
with respect, okay?</i>

07:34.390 --> 07:34.640
<b></b>I'm sorry. I just got caught up in the flow

07:36.290 --> 07:41.520
<i>But, you know, all of your super chats 
let me produce new songs and merchandise,</i>

07:41.520 --> 07:43.540
<i>so I'm really grateful!</i>

07:43.540 --> 07:47.330
<i>Thank you. I promise to use it well.</i>

07:47.650 --> 07:48.320
<i>Huh?!</i>

07:48.320 --> 07:52.170
<i>No, you've given me enough 
already! Stop! Stop it!</i>

07:52.170 --> 07:55.290
<i>Tossing money at me 
without a word is just scary!</i>

07:55.290 --> 07:59.990
<i>At least write a message of support, 
or something you want to ask me.</i>

07:59.990 --> 08:02.290
<i>I'll give you life advice if you want!</i>

08:02.290 --> 08:03.040
<b></b>Don't worry about it. Just quietly accept it.

08:04.440 --> 08:06.800
<i>Have you all gone crazy?!</i>

08:08.300 --> 08:11.370
<i>You have a test tomorrow? Good luck!</i>

08:11.370 --> 08:14.320
<i>Actually, stop watching this and go study!</i>

08:15.660 --> 08:19.020
<i>Satori-san, today's your birthday? 
Happy birthday!</i>

08:19.020 --> 08:21.500
<i>And if you need advice, 
keep the questions coming!</i>

08:23.980 --> 08:24.440
<b>NodoNodo</b>

08:23.980 --> 08:24.440
<b>NodoNodo</b>

08:24.440 --> 08:27.130
<i>I want to chase my dream of being an idol,</i>

08:27.130 --> 08:30.950
<i>but I don't have the courage to betray 
my parents' expectations.</i>

08:30.950 --> 08:33.560
<i>Oh, there's a serious one.</i>

08:33.560 --> 08:35.710
<i>NodoNodo-san, thank you!</i>

08:37.540 --> 08:39.640
<i>Hmm, yes, I see.</i>

08:39.640 --> 08:42.790
<i>I'll be cheering for you 
and your dream all the way!</i>

08:43.280 --> 08:45.710
<i>I'm sort of in the same situation.</i>

08:46.160 --> 08:48.290
<i>You know, if I wasn't doing this virtually,</i>

08:48.290 --> 08:51.720
<i>I never could've become an idol 
that this many people come to see.</i>

08:51.720 --> 08:54.970
<i>But once I discovered the virtual world, 
my path opened up before me!</i>

08:55.600 --> 08:59.480
I think it happened because 
I didn't give up on my dream.

08:59.480 --> 09:04.940
<i>This is coming straight from the source, me! 
I'll always be here cheering you on!</i>

09:04.940 --> 09:07.730
<i>And there ends my personal opinion!</i>

09:07.730 --> 09:10.850
<i>Now, do any of you have 
anything else to ask me?</i>

09:11.240 --> 09:13.380
<i>Whoa! That's a ton of replies!</i>

09:13.380 --> 09:16.920
<i>Right, then! I'll stay with 
you all until morning!</i>

09:16.920 --> 09:18.590
<i>Ask me whatever you want!</i>

09:19.900 --> 09:21.750
<i>"What color are your panties?"</i>

09:21.750 --> 09:23.900
<i>I'm a mermaid!</i>

09:23.900 --> 09:25.750
<i>I don't wear panties!</i>

09:27.110 --> 09:28.260
<i>Okay, next!</i>

09:28.840 --> 09:31.010
<i>"What's your favorite kind of sushi?"</i>

09:31.010 --> 09:35.480
<i>Well, I'm a mermaid, so I'll just say 
I like the ones that aren't fish.</i>

09:35.480 --> 09:37.260
<i>Sea urchin, crab, and ark clam!</i>

09:37.600 --> 09:41.100
<i>"In the unlikely event that you went
on a date, where would you like to go?"</i>

09:41.100 --> 09:43.770
<i>Hey! "In the unlikely event" is just rude!</i>

09:44.200 --> 09:45.480
<i>Let's see.</i>

09:45.480 --> 09:49.910
<i>In Chiba prefecture, there's a shrine 
eighteen meters underwater on the sea floor.</i>

09:49.910 --> 09:50.870
<i>Did you know that?</i>

09:50.870 --> 09:55.030
<i>I'd like to do a New Year's visit to that 
shrine and drink amazake together!</i>

10:02.190 --> 10:04.070
Earth to Miss Night Owl!

10:04.540 --> 10:06.390
Uname-sensei!

10:07.100 --> 10:08.990
Huh? What about gym class?

10:08.990 --> 10:13.150
It's already over. 
Why did you stay up so late?

10:13.150 --> 10:16.120
Oh... It's because I was watching Yorumun.

10:16.120 --> 10:17.370
Yorumun?

10:17.370 --> 10:19.810
Um... She's a VTuber!

10:19.810 --> 10:21.250
Is that a brand of chuhai?

10:21.250 --> 10:22.560
No!

10:27.560 --> 10:30.400
Well, no wonder you're in 
such a good mood today.

10:30.400 --> 10:33.920
A good mood? Me?

10:33.920 --> 10:38.330
Yes. You're always in a good mood 
the next day after you stay up late.

10:39.730 --> 10:41.580
You might be right about that.

10:41.580 --> 10:44.630
But it's not good to stay up late too often.

10:44.630 --> 10:46.080
Yes, ma'am.

10:46.080 --> 10:50.430
And as your teacher, I'm always happy to 
learn more about young people's culture.

10:50.430 --> 10:51.840
You are?

10:51.840 --> 10:57.900
So basically, these "VTubers" 
are like kamishibai performers.

10:54.970 --> 10:56.340
<b>The Tale of Yorumun</b>

10:57.900 --> 11:01.090
Sensei, weren't you listening? 
They're totally different!

11:01.090 --> 11:02.100
Oh, my.

11:02.100 --> 11:04.350
VTubers are people who livestream

11:04.350 --> 11:08.190
using an illustration or 3D model 
to represent themselves.

11:08.190 --> 11:11.340
They'll do game commentaries, 
or chat, or sing songs—

11:11.340 --> 11:12.870
all kinds of things!

11:12.870 --> 11:16.690
The people who do their character designs 
or animation are called their "parents,"

11:16.690 --> 11:19.370
and the one who voices them 
is called the "person inside"!

11:19.620 --> 11:25.530
So the person inside cheered you on, 
and that made you feel better, right?

11:25.530 --> 11:27.670
Which is why you're in a good mood.

11:27.670 --> 11:30.630
Um, yes. I guess that's right.

11:30.630 --> 11:33.340
The truth is, I was worried about you.

11:33.340 --> 11:36.030
Your parents are so successful

11:36.030 --> 11:40.310
that I thought you might be feeling too 
pressured to even have dreams of your own.

11:40.310 --> 11:41.450
Right...

11:41.450 --> 11:43.850
But it seems I didn't need to worry.

11:43.850 --> 11:46.390
I didn't know you dreamed 
of becoming an idol!

11:46.390 --> 11:47.640
Right!

11:50.050 --> 11:51.780
That's a lovely dream!

11:53.650 --> 11:56.780
I'm certain... it will come true!

11:57.880 --> 12:00.160
Pretend you didn't see that.

12:01.660 --> 12:03.030
It will!

12:03.410 --> 12:04.500
Come true!

12:05.270 --> 12:07.040
Sensei, it's all right!

12:07.040 --> 12:10.290
Wait! Don't give up on your teacher!

12:13.300 --> 12:18.160
Now that I think about it, I feel like 
I've heard of Yorumun somewhere before.

12:18.160 --> 12:20.120
Where could that have been?

12:27.310 --> 12:28.060
What?

12:28.060 --> 12:30.060
<b>Popular VTuber Himeuo Yorumun Announces Her Retirement</b>

12:28.060 --> 12:30.060
<b>A shock ran through the VTuber community today. For a
long time, Himeuo Yorumun has been entertaining fans with</b>

12:30.060 --> 12:33.660
Yorumun... is retiring?

12:41.820 --> 12:43.400
Nodoka?

12:47.130 --> 12:48.630
What's wrong?

12:53.620 --> 12:54.840
Nodoka-san?

12:56.590 --> 12:58.370
Is something wrong?

12:59.200 --> 13:02.460
If you use the formula we used 
yesterday there, it's easy to...

13:03.920 --> 13:06.580
It seems you're lacking in focus.

13:06.580 --> 13:08.850
We'll end here for today.

13:08.850 --> 13:12.350
Nodoka-san, your parents 
are brilliant doctors.

13:12.790 --> 13:16.300
The only one who can properly 
carry on their will

13:16.920 --> 13:19.110
is you.

13:20.330 --> 13:23.270
You do not have time 
for distractions right now.

13:24.120 --> 13:27.870
Please find a way to finish 
shedding your tears today.

13:38.340 --> 13:40.770
<i>It's been announced 
on her official site, too.</i>

13:41.180 --> 13:43.110
<i>This really is the end.</i>

13:45.780 --> 13:51.390
<i>Himeuo Yorumun really is gone.</i>

13:58.900 --> 14:03.100
I really wanted to become an idol.

14:06.040 --> 14:07.190
Huh?

14:11.800 --> 14:16.040
<i>This is the mermaid VTuber, Himeuo Yorumun!</i>

14:16.040 --> 14:17.200
What?!

14:18.390 --> 14:23.010
<i>Can you hear me, all you small fry? 
Is the volume all right?</i>

14:25.790 --> 14:28.240
I thought she wasn't streaming anymore.

14:29.110 --> 14:32.020
Could they have made some 
kind of mistake in the news?

14:33.190 --> 14:35.840
<i>I'm sorry I worried you.</i>

14:35.840 --> 14:39.520
<i>Everything's okay. I'm here!</i>

14:43.740 --> 14:45.530
<i>I promised, didn't I?</i>

14:46.290 --> 14:49.530
<i>I said I'd always be here cheering you on.</i>

14:50.080 --> 14:53.840
<i>The most important thing to me, 
more precious than anything else,</i>

14:53.840 --> 14:56.540
<i>is all of you who have cheered me on!</i>

15:12.660 --> 15:14.060
I'm rooting for you!

15:20.800 --> 15:23.900
You can do it! I'm rooting for you!

15:23.900 --> 15:25.380
You can do it!

15:28.820 --> 15:30.910
All right, time's up!

15:28.820 --> 15:37.080
<b></b>Math Quiz

15:31.470 --> 15:33.950
Pass your papers up to the front.

15:33.950 --> 15:37.080
I'll score them now, so you have 
ten minutes' self-study.

15:37.080 --> 15:42.090
We just finished our finals. 
Why are we taking more tests?

15:42.090 --> 15:46.600
To punish last-minute 
crammers like you, Tama.

15:47.340 --> 15:51.350
As expected, Adashino has a perfect score.

15:51.350 --> 15:53.290
Wow! That's amazing.

15:53.290 --> 15:56.850
If you all studied regularly, 
you'd get perfect scores, too.

15:56.850 --> 16:00.110
Oh, here's someone else who's working hard.

16:00.110 --> 16:01.610
Ametsuchi Nodoka!

16:01.610 --> 16:02.520
Yes?

16:02.520 --> 16:04.360
You've really put in the work!

16:09.540 --> 16:10.870
Splendid!

16:11.290 --> 16:13.620
Well done solving that one, Nodoka-san.

16:14.320 --> 16:19.660
I spoke harshly the other day, but it seems 
there was no need for me to worry.

16:19.660 --> 16:23.610
I'm certain you will surpass 
your parents' expectations.

16:24.070 --> 16:25.790
Let's do our best together.

16:26.280 --> 16:27.130
Right!

16:27.130 --> 16:29.110
Thank you!

16:31.310 --> 16:32.740
All right.

16:32.740 --> 16:35.140
Next is singing and dancing!

16:37.760 --> 16:39.370
<i>I'm rooting for you!</i>

16:39.370 --> 16:42.650
<i>I just know you can do it. 
Keep working at it!</i>

16:42.650 --> 16:43.900
I will!

16:44.690 --> 16:45.930
Yorumun!

16:46.400 --> 16:49.450
I'll do my very best! Watch me!

16:57.040 --> 17:01.180
Nodoka, you look awful. Are you all right?

17:01.850 --> 17:03.540
I'm just fine!

17:04.630 --> 17:07.750
In fact, I've never felt better!

17:07.750 --> 17:12.380
There's so much I want to do! 
I don't have time to sleep!

17:12.380 --> 17:15.470
I've stayed up for four nights in a row now!

17:15.470 --> 17:17.280
You shouldn't! You need to rest!

17:17.280 --> 17:19.060
I said I'm fine!

17:20.810 --> 17:25.700
We promised to do our 
homework together, right?

17:25.700 --> 17:26.570
But...

17:27.400 --> 17:31.070
Besides, Yorumun is cheering me on, so...

17:31.070 --> 17:33.910
no time... rest...

17:37.550 --> 17:38.830
Nodoka!

17:41.530 --> 17:42.710
Nodoka!

17:56.850 --> 17:59.350
<b>Takamagahara Hospital</b>

18:02.350 --> 18:04.850
<b>Maid Café</b>

18:06.360 --> 18:08.860
Good work today, Adashino Oto.

18:09.550 --> 18:11.860
I'm going to use the roof for a little while.

18:11.860 --> 18:13.390
Mrrow.

18:14.590 --> 18:16.110
Mrrow.

18:20.370 --> 18:25.080
We're thinking there are ten 
other cases in this town alone.

18:25.080 --> 18:29.130
If we looked nationwide, the number 
would likely be much higher.

18:29.720 --> 18:34.130
And one of these cases is Oto-chan's friend.

18:34.130 --> 18:36.190
According to the occult forums,

18:36.190 --> 18:41.890
it seems like everyone who collapsed 
was an ardent fan of Himeuo Yorumun.

18:41.890 --> 18:46.650
Nodoka mentioned her, too. She said 
that Yorumun was cheering her on.

18:46.650 --> 18:49.450
Himeuo Yorumun, huh?

18:49.450 --> 18:52.380
Her name's been all over 
the news online lately.

18:52.380 --> 18:55.370
She had a lot of fans and a good reputation,

18:55.370 --> 18:59.610
only to retire at the height of her 
popularity for undisclosed reasons.

18:59.610 --> 19:03.970
Have people been talking about 
how it was her fans who collapsed?

19:03.970 --> 19:09.400
Yes. Of course, her management has 
officially denied any connection.

19:09.400 --> 19:14.190
But Nodoka really did collapse. 
She's still in the hospital.

19:14.190 --> 19:18.200
There are rumors of Yorumun 
livestreaming even after her retirement,

19:18.550 --> 19:21.430
but apparently there isn't 
a single archived recording.

19:22.750 --> 19:27.440
Do you remember our discussion 
about tsukumogami, Sumireko-san?

19:27.440 --> 19:28.790
Of course.

19:28.790 --> 19:31.410
There's an otogizoshi—a short 
story from the Muromachi era—

19:31.410 --> 19:33.690
called the Tsukumogami Emaki.

19:31.480 --> 19:33.690
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

19:31.730 --> 19:33.690
<b>Tsukumogami Emaki</b>

19:33.690 --> 19:38.140
It says that tsukumogami are essentially 
objects that were once cared for

19:38.140 --> 19:42.530
but now have set out for revenge after 
being treated roughly and discarded.

19:42.530 --> 19:47.330
They are Curiosities that have 
changed to cause harm to humans.

19:52.960 --> 19:57.260
There's a procession of yokai 
referred to as the hyakki-yagyo,

19:57.260 --> 20:00.600
but the majority of the yokai 
depicted are tsukumogami.

20:00.600 --> 20:04.870
And all those who encounter 
the hyakki-yagyo are said to die.

20:05.570 --> 20:08.960
Tsukumogami are very unlike the 
cute little spirits you might imagine.

20:13.980 --> 20:17.090
If the vast quantity of digital data that 
humans discard at their convenience

20:17.090 --> 20:19.060
has become a tsukumogami

20:19.060 --> 20:23.330
and set out to take its revenge on humans, 
I wouldn't be surprised at all.

20:26.750 --> 20:28.750
<b>Takamagahara Hospital</b>

20:52.520 --> 20:54.520
<b>Sudden Faintings Due to Unknown Causes
\hCause Increasing Chaos Across City</b>

20:55.070 --> 20:58.280
At this rate, the number 
of victims will only increase.

20:58.280 --> 21:02.030
Ren-nii, please save Nodoka.

21:03.120 --> 21:07.270
All right. Leave it to me, Oto.

21:16.550 --> 21:20.800
<i>You say it's a cat, just a cat,</i>

21:20.800 --> 21:24.800
<i>But would a cat come 
like that, wearing geta,</i>

21:24.800 --> 21:28.810
<i>Wearing a shibori yukata?</i>

21:25.890 --> 21:28.810
You'd better prepare yourself, 
Disappearances-kun.

21:28.810 --> 21:30.830
<i>How silly of you, silly!</i>

21:30.830 --> 21:32.830
<i>How silly of you, silly!</i>

21:37.070 --> 21:41.100
<i>There are butterflies, 
dragonflies, and bush crickets</i>

21:41.100 --> 21:45.330
<i>The ones that sing in the 
mountains, the mountains,</i>

21:45.330 --> 21:49.080
<i>Are the pine crickets, bell crickets, 
and long-legged katydids</i>

21:49.080 --> 21:51.040
<i>How silly of you, silly!</i>

21:51.040 --> 21:52.970
<i>How silly of you, silly!</i>

21:52.970 --> 21:55.100
<i>And one more just for you, silly</i>

21:55.100 --> 21:57.170
<i>How silly of you, silly!</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.700
<b>A Live Performance, a Curse, and the Person Inside</b>

23:36.100 --> 23:40.020
Next time: "A Live Performance, 
a Curse, and the Person Inside."
